  "body": "Closes #6215 (remainder after the merged #6216 dual-bind work).\n\n## What\n\n`fleet-config` gains the role-socket path helpers and the per-role transport preference that #6215 asked for, following the adopted design on #5699.\n\n- **`[queue-broker]` / `[secrets-broker]` tables** with `socket` and `transport` fields. Both are `deny_unknown_fields`, so a typo is a parse error rather than silence.\n- **Socket resolution** for both roles is now `QUEUE_BROKER_SOCKET`/`SECRETS_BROKER_SOCKET` env > `[<role>] socket` > `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/fleet/<role>.sock` (when `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` is an absolute, non-empty base) > the role's historical `$HOME` default. This mirrors `broker_socket()`'s precedence; explicit overrides keep their documented relative-under-`$HOME` meaning.\n- **`Config::role_transport(role)`** parses `\"socket\" | \"tcp\"` in the `search_via` style: a preference between two working routes, never a disable lever. An unrecognized value returns `None` so the caller probes, exactly as an unknown `[search] via` falls through to the host default.\n- The proxy's historical `.cache/laptop-agent/broker.sock` is untouched — it is a compatibility contract. Only role sockets are new.\n\n## Why the runtime dir is preferred\n\n`$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` is tmpfs, per-login, and auto-cleaned, which is the right home for a runtime socket; the `$HOME` default remains the fallback for hosts without it (and keeps today's behaviour byte-for-byte when nothing is configured).\n\n## Tests\n\n`cargo test -p fleet-config` — 23 passed, 0 failed. New coverage:\n\n- `role_sockets_prefer_the_runtime_dir_then_the_home_default` — every rung of the precedence, per role name (oracle: the documented order).\n- `role_transport_parses_only_the_two_working_routes` — trimming, case, unknown value → `None`, unknown role → `None`.\n- `role_config_rejects_unknown_fields` — the deny-unknown-fields discipline holds for the new tables.\n- `role_socket_overrides_read_from_the_config_file` — absolute and relative config paths.\n\n`rustfmt --check` clean; `cargo check -p fleet-queue` still builds (the consumers call the same accessors, whose signatures are unchanged).\n\n## Deliberately not in this PR\n\nWiring the probe-based client selection into `fleet-queue`'s clients and the colocated-proxy dialing described in #5699 §3-§4. This PR lands the config surface those steps read from; the transport switch itself is a separate change with its own tests.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796759759&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7798&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7798&signature=797b3f69b612fd4040f947509e5841293d7c5484377bdf389bbaedfb878b9262\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7798?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
